["Food and drink","You order something to eat or drink.","the apple","the fish","I would like","I’d like a coffee, please.","I drink water.","I eat bread and cheese.","Regular verbs in the present","Italian verbs end in -are, -ere or -ire.","“Vorrei” (I would like) is the polite way to ask for something. It’s used far more than “voglio” (I want).","PARLARE (to speak)","PRENDERE (to take)","DORMIRE (to sleep)","parlo","prendo","dormo","parli","prendi","parla","prende","dorme","parliamo","prendiamo","dormiamo","parlate","prendete","dormite","parlano","prendono","dormono"]